-- #1383 face 2: `zwrap`'s named-field variant `Cfg` (type `Wrap`) and `acfg`'s
-- record `Cfg` share registry key `Cfg` with their two fields at opposite
-- indices.  The entry holds a value of each and names neither type.  `mkW`'s head
-- is `Wrap`, not the key, so its projections are answered by the field-owner
-- path, which selects the receiver's own declaration from the identity companion;
-- the stamp names that declaration's module, so the built binary applies `Wrap`'s
-- layout to `mkW` and `Cfg`'s to `mkZ`.
--
-- Hand-derived correct answer: `11,22,44,33`.  `mkW` is built `a = 11, b = 22`;
-- `mkZ` is built `b = 33, a = 44`.  A wrong layout on the built binary shows as a
-- transposed pair, which `medaka run` cannot show because the interpreter selects
-- fields by name.
--
-- This import order was refused at base (`Type mismatch: Wrap vs Cfg` twice); the
-- other order printed the right value.  Both orders are graded by
-- `test/import_order_fixtures/1383-variant-ctor-vs-xmod-record-field-order-invariant/`.
import zwrap.{mkW}
import acfg.{mkZ}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  putStrLn
    (intToString mkW.a
      ++ ","
      ++ intToString mkW.b
      ++ ","
      ++ intToString mkZ.a
      ++ ","
      ++ intToString mkZ.b)
